<<~ ahu #/head>>

! LarTiddlerStore ~ the contract that names no wiki

The mesh owns this shape and imports no TiddlyWiki runtime. Three stores satisfy it — a CRDT-backed
one, a canon one, a memory one — and the shape moves for none of them.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-five-layers>>

!! Five layers, one priority

| ''layer'' | ''holds'' |
|core |TW5 core, plugin and shadow tiddlers |
|canon |hostless `lares/` carriers, resident and long-lived |
|wiki |shared live wiki edits, CRDT-backed |
|user |operator private notes and personal overlays |
|session |drafts, focus state, temp tiddlers, cursors — personal |

''Priority runs core < canon < wiki < user < session'', so the nearest hand wins the view while the
furthest holds the record.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! The four hard rules

# ''The wiki layer OVERRIDES canon for the live view and MUST NOT mutate it.'' A reader sees the
working edit; the canon copy underneath stays untouched. Shadowing and writing look alike
from the view and differ entirely in what survives.
# ''The session layer MUST NOT leak into shared state.'' A draft, a temp tiddler, a cursor — each
belongs to one operator at one moment, and a sync that carried them would publish a hand mid-motion.
# ''Canon promotion stays CLOSED.'' `put` never writes to `lares/`, and it stays that way until a
Keyhive-backed proposal-and-receipt graph stands to say who promoted what and on whose authority.
Opening it earlier would put canon behind a door with no record of who walked through.
# ''Deletion MARKS, and does not remove.'' A tombstone records the deletion in live wiki state; no
hard delete happens by default, so a removal stays a claim another replica can see and reconcile
rather than an absence it must guess at.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

